ther.","‘First it grows a root, down into the soil.","Then it grows a shoot, up to the sun.’"],"alt":"A drawing shows a seed with a root going down and a shoot going up.","image":{"hash":"sha256:7b248d480bd8dee9a37c491eda9dc91ea0f5e34a3ba332cb5ae7dc20261aaf35","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:b64606d35000cc1a0fe68d4ba17f38d5c7a5efc2dac0f0dc1a704216e7b83fe7","durationMs":21440,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,8869],[8869,15613],[15613,21440]],"words":[[0,183],[183,916],[916,1832],[1832,3042],[3042,3958],[3958,4508],[4508,5534],[5534,6267],[6267,8869],[8869,9785],[9785,10152],[10152,11068],[11068,11251],[11251,12278],[12278,13011],[13011,13744],[13744,14293],[14293,15613],[15613,16346],[16346,16712],[16712,17628],[17628,17812],[17812,19021],[19021,19388],[19388,19754],[19754,20304],[20304,21440]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"So Frema watered the seed every morning. She waited and waited. Four days. Five days. She did not dig it up.","sentences":["So Frema watered the seed every morning.","She waited and waited.","Four days.","Five days.","She did not dig it up."],"alt":"A girl waters a tin each morning with a calendar on the wall.","image":{"hash":"sha256:37bf338855350b46419144644b4da8f2dbd1b1c604926e28a9181aeb1a12bc44","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:ae085e809f639eabd68df18a005890699f0002e79e25b02b0749df6cb1a9d047","durationMs":14920,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5456],[5456,8651],[8651,10339],[10339,12026],[12026,14920]],"words":[[0,301],[301,1055],[1055,2110],[2110,2562],[2562,3165],[3165,3918],[3918,5456],[5456,5908],[5908,6812],[6812,7264],[7264,8651],[8651,9253],[9253,10339],[10339,10941],[10941,12026],[12026,12479],[12479,12931],[12931,13383],[13383,13835],[13835,14136],[14136,14920]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"One morning, Frema looked in the tin. A tiny green shoot was pushing up out of the soil! ‘It grew!’ she shouted.","sentences":["One mo